Net cash provided by operating activities was $1,291,951 for the fiscal year ended March 31, 2026, which primarily consisted of the following:

• net income of $1,904,661 for the fiscal year ended March 31, 2026;

• an increase in accounts receivable of $2,375,433, primarily due to the timing and concentration of sales and service revenues in the fourth fiscal quarter, an increased proportion of wholesale and corporate service contracts granted credit terms of up to 90 days, longer collection periods resulting from broader macroeconomic and real estate market conditions in China, and the appreciation of the RMB against the U.S. dollar, partially offset by an allowance for expected credit losses of $301,699; as of October 31, 2026, approximately $3,222,415, or 83.1%, of the March 31, 2026 accounts receivable balance has been subsequently collected in cash, and the remaining net balance (excluding the allowance for expected credit losses) is expected to be collected by December 31, 2026;

• an increase in inventories of $449,610, because we increased the stockpile of electric appliance products in anticipation of continued sales growth;

• an increase in accounts payable of $324,072 from third-party suppliers, partially offset by a decrease in accounts payable from a related party supplier of $30,510; we have not received the invoices from suppliers as of the applicable fiscal…
